-- wra3-sch10.l4: the Welfare Reform Act 2012 (United Kingdom), 2012 c. 5, Schedule 10 (personal independence payment:
-- transitional). Part wra3, layer 1. Written from inputs/ukpga-2012-5.txt, a plain-text rendering of legislation.gov.uk
-- (version 2026-07-01), not the official text.
--
-- The paragraph numbers of Schedule 10 are not printed in the text. They are counted by cross-heading (General 1,
-- Claims before the appointed day 2, Claims after the appointed day 3, Awards 4, Supplementary 5), as PLAN.md section 5
-- does, and para 1(1) is cited by the Act itself (paragraph 2(1) and 3(1) say "paragraph 1(1)").
-- Only paragraph 1(2) carries a definition. Paragraph 1(1) and paragraphs 2 to 5 say what regulations under section 93
-- "may in particular" provide: they are regulation-making powers and are inert (reason 2); the claims, awards and
-- transitions they allow are made by regulations that are not among the sources.

§ `sch 10 para 1(2) the appointed day`

-- "the appointed day" means the day appointed for the coming into force of section 77 (section 150(3)).
-- src:3360 | (2) In this Schedule “the appointed day” means the day appointed for the coming into force of section 77.
@ref sch 10 para 1(2) (src:3360)
GIVEN `the day appointed for the coming into force of section 77` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`sch 10 para 1(2) the appointed day` MEANS
    `s 150(3) the day appointed for the coming into force of the provision` `the day appointed for the coming into force of section 77`

@ref sch 10 para 1(2) (src:3360)
GIVEN `the date` IS A DATE
      `the day appointed for the coming into force of section 77` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 10 para 1(2) the date is on or after the appointed day` MEANS
    `s 150(3) the provision is in force on the date` `the date` `the day appointed for the coming into force of section 77`
